Add({
	id = "alterac-mountains",
	title = "Alterac Mountains",
	aliases = { "Alterac", "Kingdom of Alterac" },
	faction = "Contested",
	continent = "Eastern Kingdoms",
	maps = { 1416 },
	zone = "Alterac Mountains",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "zone" },
		{ type = "map" },
	},
	regionKind = "zone",
	kind = "region",
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Alterac Mountains rise north of the {link:hillsbrad-foothills}Hillsbrad Foothills{/link}, a wall of snow and grey stone between the shores of {red:lordamere-lake}Lordamere Lake{/red} and the dead lands of the Plaguelands. Once they were a kingdom of their own. Its capital lies broken in the high passes, and its name is still spoken as a curse in the courts of men, for Alterac betrayed the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} in its darkest hour. Now the mountains belong to whoever can hold them: exiled nobles and their cutthroats, ogres crowned with stolen relics, wizards, assassins, orcs and dwarves.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[Alterac was one of the city-states that the humans of {link:arathor}Arathor{/link} founded in the wilderness after the death of King {link:thoradin}Thoradin{/link}, when their empire grew beyond the walls of {link:stromgarde-keep}Strom{/link}. It prospered on the roads through the mountains, and in time it became one of the human kingdoms that divided the old empire between them. The Perenolde family ruled it from a castle in the high city. The farms of the {link:the-uplands}Uplands{/link} fed it, and the magi of {link:dalaran}Dalaran{/link} were its neighbors across the lake.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[The {link:syndicate}Syndicate{/link} holds much of the old kingdom. Its lords have made the ghost town of {link:strahnbrad}Strahnbrad{/link} their fortress and the {link:the-uplands}Uplands{/link} their hunting ground, and {link:lord-aliden-perenolde}Lord Aliden Perenolde{/link} keeps his court in a manor on the lakeshore. Strangers in black robes stand at his side. The ruined capital belongs to the {link:crushridge-ogres}Crushridge{/link} ogres and their warlord {link:mug-thol}Mug'thol{/link}, who wears a crown that {link:sylvanas-windrunner}the Dark Lady{/link} wants back. In the west, {link:dalaran}Dalaran{/link} stands rebuilt, and its great barrier has fallen. In the east, the assassins of {link:ravenholdt-manor}Ravenholdt{/link} watch the Syndicate from their hidden manor. At the mouth of {link:alterac-valley}Alterac Valley{/link}, dwarves of {link:kingdom-of-ironforge}Ironforge{/link} and orcs of the {link:frostwolf-clan}Frostwolf clan{/link} gather soldiers for a war of their own. {link:southshore}Southshore{/link} and {link:tarren-mill}Tarren Mill{/link} both send hunters into the snows, each for its own reasons.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Inhabitants",
			text = [=[• {b}The {link:syndicate}Syndicate{/link}.{/b} Fallen nobles of Alterac, with the thieves, footpads and shadow mages who serve them.
• {b}The {link:crushridge-ogres}Crushridge{/link} ogres.{/b} An {link:ogres}ogre{/link} warband that has taken the ruined capital and dug a mound in the hills beyond it.
• {b}The magi of {link:dalaran}Dalaran{/link}.{/b} The {link:kirin-tor}Kirin Tor{/link} and their guards, workers and bound elementals.
• {b}The Assassin's League.{/b} The rogues of {link:ravenholdt-manor}Ravenholdt{/link}, who answer to no king.
• {b}The {link:stormpike-guard}Stormpike Guard{/link} and the {link:frostwolf-clan}Frostwolf Clan{/link}.{/b} {link:dwarves}Dwarves{/link} and orcs at war over {link:alterac-valley}Alterac Valley{/link}.
• {b}Beasts.{/b} Yetis in the caves, mountain lions on the slopes, and bears on the lower hills.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Kingdom.{/b} For centuries Alterac was a small but proud realm of the north, often at odds with its neighbor {link:stromgarde-keep}Stromgarde{/link}.
• {b}The {link:second-war}Second War{/link}.{/b} King {link:aiden-perenolde}Aiden Perenolde{/link} doubted the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} from the first. When the {link:horde}Horde{/link} reached his mountains, he made a secret pact with {link:orgrim-doomhammer}Orgrim Doomhammer{/link} and opened the southern passes. The orcs crossed in days rather than months and laid siege to the capital of {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}.
• {b}The Fall.{/b} When the betrayal was known, the armies of the Alliance marched on Alterac. King {link:terenas-menethil}Terenas Menethil{/link} deposed Perenolde and held him prisoner in his own palace. The kingdom never rose again, and its people scattered.
• {b}The Plague.{/b} In the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}, the {link:scourge}Scourge{/link} swept through Lordaeron, and {link:archimonde}Archimonde{/link} cast down {link:dalaran}Dalaran{/link} across the lake. What order remained in the mountains died with them.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Lore of the Mountains",
			text = [=[• The Perenolde Tiara, an heirloom of the old royal house, was made by the jewelers of {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link} and set with emeralds. It was lost when Alterac fell. An {link:ogres}ogre{/link} mage of the {link:crushridge-ogres}Crushridge{/link} is said to carry it now.
• The magistrate of {link:southshore}Southshore{/link} was murdered by assassins who were never found. His successor believes the {link:syndicate}Syndicate{/link} hired them.
• Hunters say that a great yeti called Frostmaw roams the heights above {link:growless-cave}Growless Cave{/link}.]=],
		},
	},
})

